ambmpega.library: changes
=========================

1.3 (21 November 2026)
----------------------

- dct32 in 68k assembler (src/dct32_68k.s), both builds, written from
  libmad's C by tools/gen_dct32.py (on tools/gen68k.py): the same samples. ambmpega.library's
  products are one MULS.L 32 x 32 -> 64 each by the constant shifted so
  that the high register is the result. A frame of 128 kbit/s MP3: 4.94 M
  68020 cycles -> 4.82 M; Layer II 4.07 M -> 3.94 M. ambmpega060.library:
  850 k instructions a frame -> 788 k (MP3), 587 k -> 526 k (Layer II).
- Layer III's IMDCT for long blocks in 68k assembler too, both builds
  (src/layer3_68k.s, tools/gen_layer3.py): imdct36 with the normal
  window in one, the same samples. MP3: 4.82 M 68020 cycles -> 4.58 M;
  ambmpega060.library 788 k instructions -> 749 k.
- In all, a frame of 128 kbit/s MP3: ambmpega.library 4.94 M 68020 cycles
  -> 4.58 M (-7%); ambmpega060.library 850 k instructions -> 749 k (-12%),
  which on a real 68060 at 50 MHz (20.3 ms a frame in 1.2) should be
  about 17.9 ms. Layer II: 4.07 M -> 3.94 M; 587 k -> 526 k (-10%).
- make prof INSTR=1: instructions by function (tools/prof_instr.py), and
  VARIANT=060 profiles the 68060's build.

1.2 (21 November 2026)
----------------------

- ambmpega060.library, the 68060's build: libmad's fixed-point products
  made from 32-bit multiplies (FPM_68060, third_party/libmad/fixed.h), as
  a 68060 has no MULS.L 32 x 32 -> 64 and 68060.library emulates each one
  (about 19,700 a frame of 128 kbit/s MP3). The same accuracy (83 dB);
  its samples within a step of ambmpega.library's. make test decodes the
  fixtures through both, each against its own expected CRCs and the two
  against each other, and checks the 68060's build has no 64-bit multiply
  or divide. ambmpega.library itself is unchanged but for its version.

1.1 (17 November 2026)
----------------------

- Renamed ambmpega.library (was amcempega.library), as AmigaMCE became
  Ambiance: AMBMPEGANAME and AMBMPEGAVERSION in libraries/mpega.h. The
  functions are unchanged.

1.0 (15 November 2026)
----------------------

- Medium and low quality (MPEGA_QUALITY_MEDIUM, LOW): the synthesis
  window's products 16-bit, one MULS.W each: 9% fewer 68020 cycles for
  MP3 (4.46 M a frame of 128 kbit/s stereo), 11% for Layer II (3.90 M),
  at 70 dB from a float decoder (high: 83 dB; mpega 2.4's best: 34 dB for
  MP3, 56 dB for Layer II).
- 22 and 11 kHz: the half-rate synthesis window in assembler too.
- MPGA_decode_to, the library's own: each frame straight into the
  program's ring buffers as 16-bit (two buffers, or interleaved for
  AHI), 8-bit for Paula (dithered or not) or Paula's 14 bits (a high
  byte and 6 more bits a channel), with each channel's peak and the
  clipped counted on the way: no copying or converting after it. The
  writers in 68k assembler (src/out_68k.s), about 43 68020 cycles a
  sample, the same bytes as the host's C.
- The synthesis window in 68k assembler (src/synth_68k.s), the same
  samples as libmad's C.
- Mono from stereo synthesised once (the channels averaged before the
  synthesis); at 22 and 11 kHz Layer III's upper subbands left out.

- First version: libmad 0.15.1b (with Debian's security fixes) behind
  mpega.library's seven functions, a 68020 build with each fixed-point
  multiply one MULS.L 32 x 32 -> 64. MPEG-1, 2 and 2.5, Layers I-III; Xing
  and Info headers (the length, the seeking table; the Info frame not
  played); ID3v2 tags passed over; 22 and 11 kHz output, stereo as mono,
  the loudness; the bitstream hook or a file; a stack of its own.
